(BAS-17 - inside an OPEN clause a blank line is not cosmetic: it
 force-closes every clause still open, including an enclosing function
 definition. Here one blank line closes the nested If, the While, and the
 function `report` all at once, so `Print "top"` is a top-level statement
 and runs once rather than three times inside the loop.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox BAS-17.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   tick 0
   marked
   tick 1
   tick 2
   top
)
To report.
    a number called tick is 0.
    While tick is less than 3,
        if tick is equal to 1 then,
            print "marked".
        print "tick {tick}",
        increment tick.

report.
Print "top".
